<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clemens Wenceslaus of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1739">1739</a>–<a href="/years/1812">1812</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clemens Wenceslaus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> was a son of the Elector of Saxony who became Prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a> in 1768 and in the same year the last Archbishop-Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a>. He fled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-occupation-of-the-netherlands">French revolutionary armies</a> in 1794, and in 1803 his electorate was dissolved. He kept the see of Augsburg until its secularisation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clemens-wenceslaus-of-saxony.jpg" alt="Clemens Wenceslaus of Saxony" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Palauenc05 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trier_Stadtmuseum_Clemens_Wenzeslaus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
